00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Phillip: When providing information to customers
it is not only good to know what you are talking

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.730
about, but you should also be aware of the
different rules associated with that information.

00:00:10.559 --> 00:00:13.489
There are three categories of
rule you need to follow, these are

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:16.449
Legal, Organizational, and Ethical.

00:00:17.309 --> 00:00:21.509
These rules are put in place to protect
customers by making sure the information

00:00:21.509 --> 00:00:24.250
they’re given is accurate and not misleading.

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:29.610
• Maddy: Legal rules are rules you’re required
to follow by law, and if you don’t follow

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:35.139
these you may be liable to criminal penalties
like fines or even a prison sentence.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:40.680
• Organisational rules are the rules your
organization requires you to follow.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:45.850
They’re set by the organization, and although
you might not be breaking the law, by not

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:51.319
following them, you could face disciplinary
proceedings, or even the sack if you don’t.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:57.970
• Ethical rules are rules that aren’t in
law or enforced by your organization, but

00:00:57.970 --> 00:00:59.590
which are still the right thing to do.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:04.560
Phillip: It is also important to note
that sometimes the same rule will be a

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:10.309
legal, organizational, and ethical all
at once, whereas other might only fall

00:01:10.309 --> 00:01:12.089
into one or two of these categories.

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:17.000
So, let’s look at some examples of the
rules that may relate to your role.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:18.570
Maddy: Legal

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:23.830
It’s against the law to deliberately give
false or misleading information to a customer.

00:01:24.389 --> 00:01:29.500
For example, if you’re selling a health
product and make wild claims and exaggerations

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:34.240
about what it can do, like claiming it can
cure serious illnesses, but you know that

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.790
it can’t, then you’re committing fraud.

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:42.280
This is a criminal offence, and the
consequences can be severe, especially

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:43.690
if people are hurt as a result.

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:47.949
There are also laws about the type of
information that you can share with a

00:01:47.949 --> 00:01:53.600
customer, such as personal or sensitive
information about another customer or

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:55.880
colleague which might be legally protected.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.770
Phillip: Organisational rules

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:04.009
Organisational rules often cover things
like maintaining discipline and promoting a

00:02:04.039 --> 00:02:06.259
particular kind of culture in the workplace.

00:02:06.719 --> 00:02:11.140
For example, if you worked as part of
the team in a retail environment, there’s

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:12.720
probably a dress code you must follow.

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:18.299
This is important to maintain the integrity of
the brand, as you are the face of the business.

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:23.220
When providing information to customers,
the organization might require its people

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:25.810
to use a particular style and tone of voice.

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:30.239
This is usually to try and enhance
their reputation and make their product

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:32.320
or service seem more attractive.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:37.940
For example, they might require their people to
make sure they mention certain features about

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:42.730
a product or service, early in the conversation
with a customer to try and get their attention.

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:48.540
Or there might be a rule that you should mention
other products or services, that complement

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.359
the one the customer is interested in.

00:02:51.559 --> 00:02:56.599
Organisational rules will also require their
people to follow all the legal rules associated

00:02:56.599 --> 00:02:58.929
with their role in the organisation too.

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:01.010
Maddy: Ethical rules

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:06.420
There are ways of communicating information
with customers which are legal, permitted by

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:09.380
organizational rules, but are not always ethical.

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:13.799
For example, you might encourage a
customer to believe that a particular

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:16.079
product or service is very popular.

00:03:16.789 --> 00:03:21.940
This can be done by just providing smaller bits
of information, so they form a particular picture,

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:27.069
like mentioning you’ve recently had to order
more stock of a product as it is selling out.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:32.380
This might be true, but you could be presenting
it to the customer in such a way, to make

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:37.780
them think that this product is popular and
in high demand, which might not be the case.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:40.620
You may even get commission
for the amount you sell.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:46.690
So, this isn’t technically lying, and you’re not
making false claims about the product or service,

00:03:47.219 --> 00:03:50.249
but it is still deceitful and isn’t ethical.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:56.860
Likewise, using highly charged emotional
language in a negotiation, or expressing

00:03:57.020 --> 00:04:02.390
exaggerated sadness, if it looks like the
customer is walking away, isn’t illegal and

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:07.590
might not be breaking any organizational
rules, but it isn’t very ethical, because

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:09.840
you’re manipulating the customers emotions.

00:04:10.529 --> 00:04:15.489
Phillip: By making sure you follow all legal,
organizational, and ethical rules, you help to

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:20.770
encourage a more open, honest, and safe working
environment for your team and for customers.

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:25.739
It’s especially important to remember
that breaching these rules, can also put

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:29.840
customers safety in jeopardy, and there
can be severe consequences for this.

